@packages/sigilc/compiler.sigil from SigilSemanticCompiler import { CompilerCommands }

component SigilImplementationClaims {
  goal {
    Apply *ImplementationLaws* to caller supplied readings of whole files and stored design claims, reporting whether selected implementation scope satisfies the design or has drift.
  }

  constraints {
    *CodeVocabulary* The unit is a whole file. No language parser or source annotation supplies a mapping, and file location alone does not establish component membership. Keep unmapped elements visible.

    *FileReadings* Accept only data rows within the presented names and file binding. A bad row refuses that file's answer; an empty or elementless answer leaves it unread.
  }

  cases {
    CodeVocabulary A code element may be mapped to a component and a Tag it delivers. A test mapping records what it exercises, but does not establish production membership or delivery.

    *FileRequests* Report a selected empty file, skipped symlink, automatically excluded design file, and unpresentable file as distinct selection outcomes.
  }

  interface {
    CodeVocabulary Publish accepted row shapes, element kinds, action relations, measure names, and vocabulary generation for implementation readings. Observation rows are separate from interpreter supplied mappings.

    *CodeGuidance* Publish compiled code reading guidance with its own fingerprint and vocabulary generation. Extract copies only to a named path outside the workspace under validation.

    FileRequests Present each selected, readable whole file with its source bytes, design names, admitted design claims, relevant Facet context, and code guidance. Bind each request to path and content, names, effective selection, guidance, and vocabulary generation. Report empty, skipped, excluded, and unpresentable files separately.

    *AlignCommands* CompilerCommands Provide align prepare, align ingest, and align check in sigilc. Prepare reads workspace selection and refuses a nonempty output directory. Ingest admits one file against its binding. Check reuses fresh readings and reports which files need new readings. No command launches an interpreter.

    ImplementationLaws Compare admitted code observations with scoped design commitments. Derive component membership, Tag delivery, dependencies through observed actions, exclusions, required state owners, exclusive ownership, and numeric budgets. Count rightful members as owners and keep unmapped code visible. Test elements never establish production delivery or ownership.

    *AlignCheck* Check the complete linked design before comparing the selected implementation scope. Return Incomplete for incomplete or disjoint design, unread code, or unpresentable files; Drift for disagreements, undesigned files or elements, and unanswered promises. With complete inputs and no alignment findings, return Closed when the linked design has no findings, or Converged when it has findings without contradictions or ownership conflicts. Closed and Converged exit zero; Drift and Incomplete exit one. No command launches an interpreter.

    *LocatedFindings* Write a versioned workspace report and judgment context under claims. Findings identify the law, supporting design claims, code rows, and locations in whole-file source bytes. Include incomplete reasons, unread files, undesigned code, unanswered promises, selection details, and identity data.

    FileReadings Store admitted readings by content, code guidance, and vocabulary identities so path renames can reuse them. Request new readings when code, cited names, component membership promises, or relevant undesigned names change. Re-ingesting an identical answer makes no write.
  }
}

