  room lock,
  transactional entry,
}
@shared.sigil from SharedKernel import {
  30-minute grid,
  local span,
  UTC instant,
}

component Availability {
  goal {
    Let a room owner say when a room is open, and let other modules ask for that open time over a date range.
  }

  state {
    Availability owns each *weekly window* of a room, which is a weekday with a local start and end on the 30-minute grid in the room timezone. The end may be 24:00, and a weekday may have any number of them.

    Availability owns each *blackout*, which covers one whole room-local date of a room.

    The *open time* of a room is its weekly window values minus its blackout dates, expressed as UTC instant ranges.
  }

  logic {
    Computing open time for a room over a local date range takes five steps. Step one reads the room timezone and the weekly window values of the room. Step two collects, for each concrete local date in the range, the weekly window values of its weekday as local span values. Step three drops every date that has a blackout. Step four hands the local span values to SharedKernel, which converts them to UTC instant ranges, drops slots inside a daylight-saving gap, and merges adjacent ranges, including 24:00 joining 00:00 of the next day. Step five returns the merged UTC instant ranges as the open time to the caller.
  }

  constraints {
    The weekly window values of one weekday must not overlap. Adjacent windows are allowed and merge.

    A weekly window must start and end on the 30-minute grid, and an off-grid time is rejected.

    The open time must be computed per concrete local date and then converted to instants, never precomputed in UTC.

    Only the room owner may add or remove a weekly window or blackout, and each edit must run inside the transaction that Booking opens under the room lock and passes to the transactional entry of Availability, which only Booking may import and which never opens the lock itself.

    An edit to a weekly window or blackout must not sweep, decline, or cancel any booking. The sweep that follows an edit belongs to Booking, in the same transaction.

    Availability depends on Rooms for the room timezone and room owner, and on SharedKernel for the conversion of a local span.
  }

  cases {
    Weekly window values on Monday from 09:00 to 12:00 and from 11:00 to 15:00 are rejected as overlapping, while 09:00 to 12:00 and 12:00 to 15:00 are accepted and merge in the open time.

    A weekly window starting at 09:15 is rejected as off the 30-minute grid.

    Adding a blackout for a date removes that date's open time and leaves the next date unaffected, and removing the blackout restores the open time.

    Given weekly window values on Friday from 18:00 to 24:00 and on Saturday from 00:00 to 02:00, the open time is one continuous span from Friday 18:00 to Saturday 02:00.

    A signed-in user who is not the room owner cannot add or remove a weekly window or blackout.

    A blackout on a past date is accepted and changes no open time that can still matter.
  }

  interface {
    Availability provides the edit of a weekly window and a blackout through its own transactional entry, for Booking's editing workflow to use.

    Availability provides the open time of a room over a local date range as UTC instant ranges, to Booking and Calendar.

    Availability provides the blackout dates of a room, for Calendar to show to the room owner.

    Availability provides the current weekly window and blackout entries of a room to its room owner, so the manage page can show them.
  }

  decisions {
    Weekly windows plus whole-day blackouts were chosen over weekly-only hours and over date overrides that can also open time, because they give enough expressiveness with one precedence rule.

    Adjacent weekly windows merge instead of being rejected, since only a true overlap is ambiguous.
  }
}

