component SharedKernel {
  goal {
    Give every module one agreed way to measure and compare time, so that a booking ending at 10:00 never conflicts with one starting at 10:00 and no module holds a different idea of now.
  }

  logic {
    Resolving a requested boundary in a zone takes three steps. Step one checks that the local time is on the *30-minute grid*. Step two rejects a *nonexistent local time*. Step three resolves an *ambiguous local time* to its earlier occurrence and returns the resulting *UTC instant* to the caller.

    Converting a *local span* to instants takes two steps. Step one turns each 30-minute slot of the span into a UTC instant range and drops every slot inside a daylight-saving gap. Step two merges adjacent ranges, so a span ending at 24:00 joins one starting at 00:00 the next day, and returns the merged *half-open range* values to the caller.
  }

  constraints {
    The time and domain-error rules of SharedKernel must not import database access or framework code, so every rule on a local span or UTC instant stays a pure function.

    Every check against the current time must read the *clock* and never the database now(), so tests can create an item before its start and act after it.

    A half-open range includes its start and excludes its end, so two ranges that meet at one instant do not overlap.

    A boundary must lie on the 30-minute grid, and 24:00 is allowed only as the end of a local span.
  }

  cases {
    A local time of 09:00 or 09:30 is on the 30-minute grid, and 09:15 is rejected.

    The half-open range 09:00 to 10:00 and the half-open range 10:00 to 11:00 do not overlap, while 09:00 to 10:30 and 10:00 to 11:00 do.

    In America/New_York, 02:00 on the spring-forward date is a nonexistent local time, and 01:30 on the fall-back date is an ambiguous local time that resolves to the earlier UTC instant.

    A local span from 01:00 to 04:00 on the spring-forward date in America/New_York yields two real hours of UTC instant ranges.

    In Asia/Kolkata a local span still aligns to the 30-minute grid in local time even though local :00 is UTC :30, and Australia/Lord_Howe's 30-minute daylight-saving shift yields correct spans.
  }

  interface {
    SharedKernel provides the clock to every command and query. Server actions pass the system clock, and tests pass a fixed one.

    SharedKernel provides the checks on the 30-minute grid and the resolution of a nonexistent local time or ambiguous local time to a UTC instant.

    SharedKernel provides the conversion of a local span to merged half-open range values of UTC instant.

    SharedKernel provides a *domain error* for each expected failure, such as a lost race or a rejected boundary, so callers map it to a user message without exposing internals.
  }

  decisions {
    Time uses Temporal through temporal-polyfill because daylight-saving arithmetic is central to the domain, and moving to native Temporal waits for a runtime that ships it.

    The 30-minute grid and half-open ranges were chosen over any-minute ranges and whole-day bookings to keep the calendar tidy and back-to-back bookings conflict-free.
  }
}

