          SharedKernel provides a *domain error* for each expected failure, such as a lost race or a rejected boundary, so callers map it to a user message without exposing internals.
  }

  decisions {
          Time uses Temporal through temporal-polyfill because daylight-saving arithmetic is central to the domain, and moving to native Temporal waits for a runtime that ships it.

          The 30-minute grid and half-open ranges were chosen over any-minute ranges and whole-day bookings to keep the calendar tidy and back-to-back bookings conflict-free.
  }
}

@identity.sigil from Identity import { signed-in user }
@rooms.sigil from Rooms import {
  transactional entry,
  room timezone,
  room list,
  archived room,
}
@availability.sigil from Availability import { weekly window, blackout }
@booking.sigil from Booking import {
  booking request,
  booking workflow,
  decline cause,
}
@shared.sigil from SharedKernel import { domain error }

component Slotted {
  goal {
    Slotted is a single signed-in app where any user can own rooms and rent other people's rooms, with the owner approving each request and the calendar never showing overlapping confirmed bookings.
  }

  constraints {
    Slotted must be one Next.js app made of the modules Identity, Rooms, Availability, Booking, and Calendar plus the kernel SharedKernel, which is not a module and which any module may use, where each module exposes one *module public entry* and no other module may import its internals. Rooms and Availability also expose a transactional entry beside it.

    The allowed module dependencies are exactly Booking on Availability and Rooms, Availability on Rooms, Rooms on Identity, and Calendar on Booking, Availability, and Rooms, with no cycles. The app imports only a module public entry.

    Slotted depends on Identity for the signed-in user and on SharedKernel for the domain error, and reaches every other module only through its module public entry.

    Only Booking may import the transactional entry of Rooms or of Availability, so the app reaches archive, unarchive, room timezone change, and availability edits only through a booking workflow.

    Every page and every *server action* except sign-up and sign-in must call requireUser to obtain the signed-in user, because the proxy redirect on the session cookie is optimistic and not a security boundary.

    Every server action must re-verify the session and ownership, invoke one module command or booking workflow, map each domain error to a distinct form message that leaks no internals, and then refresh the page.

    Every module must deliver each expected refusal, such as not allowed, an invalid room timezone, an overlapping or off-grid window, or unauthenticated, as a domain error.

    Slotted fixes its *technology stack* as Next.js 16.3.7 or later with the App Router on Node 22 with TypeScript 6.0 and cacheComponents off, Postgres 18 with Drizzle and the pg driver using generate and migrate only, Better Auth with email and password, and temporal-polyfill for time.

    Slotted must not handle payments, pricing, deposits, reviews, messaging, or organizations, and the status of a booking request is visible in the app only, with no email, push, or real-time notification.
  }

  cases {
    A signed-out visit to a room page redirects to sign-in, and a server action submitted without a session is refused and changes nothing.

    An owner creates a room with a timezone, weekly windows, and a blackout, and the room appears in another signed-in user's list.

    A renter picks a range on a room calendar and submits it, and the booking request appears as Pending or the form shows the reason it was rejected.

    The owner approves one of two overlapping requests, and both parties see the new status of each booking request in the app.

    A renter withdraws a pending booking request and may submit the same range again, or either party cancels a confirmed one and the time becomes requestable again.

    A signed-in user who does not own a room and submits its manage-page actions is refused, and the room timezone and every booking request stay unchanged.
  }

  interface {
    Slotted offers each signed-in user a room list, a room creation page, and a room calendar with a request form.

    Slotted offers the owner of a room a manage page for its details, room timezone, each weekly window, each blackout, archive, and unarchive, which also reaches each archived room of that owner, and an inbox of each booking request on its rooms.

    Slotted offers each renter a page of each booking request they hold, with its current status and decline cause.

    Slotted offers sign-up and sign-in pages that need no session, while every other page requires a signed-in user.
  }

  decisions {
    A modular monolith with one Sigil design per module was chosen so each module's responsibility, ownership of its Tags, and interface can be reviewed before its code exists.

    Next.js is pinned at 16.3.7 or later for the 2026-09-30 security release, and TypeScript stays on 6.0 because typescript-eslint does not yet support 7.

    Better Auth and Drizzle were chosen over Auth.js, Lucia, and Prisma, which is unsupported by Better Auth at its current release candidate.

    Slotted is a reference app for exercising Sigil design and a build pipeline, so behavioral coherence outranks market fit, and deployment and production observability are deferred.
  }
}

